{
  "id": "tomodachi-life-2013",
  "kind": "game",
  "title": "Tomodachi Life",
  "subtitle": "Nintendo SPD · Nintendo 3DS",
  "summary": "Tomodachi Life is Nintendo's Nintendo 3DS social simulation about an island of Mii characters. The player creates or imports its residents, adjusts their voices and personalities, then watches them establish friendships, arguments and romances. A cast can resemble friends, relatives, celebrities or a deliberately unlikely mixture of all three. The island's daily life gives those familiar faces unpredictable combinations. Instead of assigning a fixed role to each resident, the player attends to requests and discovers what the group does when left to develop relationships of its own.",
  "body": [
    "Tomodachi Life is Nintendo's Nintendo 3DS social simulation about an island of Mii characters. The player creates or imports its residents, adjusts their voices and personalities, then watches them establish friendships, arguments and romances. A cast can resemble friends, relatives, celebrities or a deliberately unlikely mixture of all three. The island's daily life gives those familiar faces unpredictable combinations. Instead of assigning a fixed role to each resident, the player attends to requests and discovers what the group does when left to develop relationships of its own.",
    "A Mii might want food, different clothes, company or help resolving a disagreement. Meeting that request changes the resident's mood and can open another interaction. Personality and relationships supply context, so the same item may be received differently by another person. The player's influence stays close to those immediate needs. The pleasure often comes from the gap between the person represented and the situation the game invents, with text-to-speech voices making an unexpected remark sound as though it belongs to that particular resident.",
    "Shops, public places and performances draw the Miis outside their apartments. Songs can be arranged with customised lyrics, turning the resident cast into performers for a miniature show. Dreams and other scenes provide further glimpses of their peculiar lives. The overseas release followed in 2014 after extensive work on localisation and speech, adapting details for different audiences. Tomodachi Life turns character creation into an ongoing source of comedy: a face takes only a little time to make, but the island keeps finding another situation in which to place it."
  ],
